 "findings": [
  "Original games separate models; classics don't. Every model scored 11-15% on Zork I, while Skerrin Light scores ranged from 1 to 50 (out of 50).",
  "Only GPT-6.1 Sol fully solved Skerrin Light (50/50 in 146 turns). Gemini 4 Argon and Claude Sonnet 5.5 were still scoring when the 150-turn limit hit; the game's suggested limit is 300.",
  "Variance is real: Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite scored 23, 30 and 41 on three runs of the same game. Use three or more runs before ranking close models.",
  "Following the output format is part of the test. DeepSeek V4 Flash kept inventing the game's replies after its own command, so 64% of its commands were invalid.",
  "Cost per point varies about 50x: GLM 5.3 Flash played four games for $0.04, while Gemini 4 Argon spent $1.80 on two."
